Single Value Decomposition (SVD)
A = USV^T
    U is orthognal: U^T*U = Im --> m x m
    S rectangular diagonal with singular values σ1 ≥ ... ≥ σr > 0 on first r diagonal entries, zeroes elsewhere --> m x n
    V is orthogonal matrix --> n x n 

SVD stores all m left-singular vectors and all n right-singular vectors, even though
only the first r correspond to nonzero singular values

